### 12. Success Criteria

The project shall be considered successfully demonstrated when the team can:

1. Run a FreeRTOS-based embedded application on the STM32.
2. Collect runtime telemetry from the target.
3. Transfer telemetry to the PC.
4. Display live system performance.
5. Store and visualize historical telemetry.
6. Detect and record controlled abnormal conditions.
7. Capture selected Cortex-M fault information.
8. Verify firmware integrity.
9. Perform trend or anomaly analysis where implemented.
10. Generate an industrial-style diagnostic report.
11. Export the report as a PDF.
12. Demonstrate the complete data flow from STM32 to final diagnostic output.

### 13. Project Boundary

CortexGuard is a development, testing, diagnostics, and research prototype.

It is not intended to replace certified safety, debugging, security, or automotive/medical/aerospace development tools.

Predictive analysis provides engineering trend estimates and shall not be interpreted as guaranteed future system behavior.

